cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MM Eco Slith3r: Multimaterial Toolpath Generator for Eco-Efficient Composite 3D Printing"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Amani
    given-names: Muhammad
    affiliation: "Shaping Matter Lab, Delft University of Technology"
    email: m.amani@tudelft.nl
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/Muhamadamani/MMEcoSlith3r"
url: "https://github.com/Muhamadamani/MMEcoSlith3r"
abstract: >
  MM Eco Slith3r is a multimaterial toolpath generator for eco-efficient
  composite 3D printing. It converts topology optimisation results (VTU files
  from MMEcoTopOpt) into G-code for dual-material FDM printers, generating
  continuous, orientation-aligned toolpaths for two materials. Includes both
  a MATLAB implementation and a Python port with a cross-platform GUI.
keywords:
  - multimaterial 3D printing
  - topology optimisation
  - toolpath generation
  - composite manufacturing
  - eco-efficient
  - FDM
  - G-code
license: MIT
date-released: "2025-01-01"
